{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pulls/15","id":4233345149,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSF2Y5878U7h9","html_url":"https://github.com/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pull/15","diff_url":"https://github.com/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pull/15.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pull/15.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/issues/15","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pulls/15/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pulls/15/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/issues/15/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diondavid1998/StreamScout/statuses/fb5cf7ccf5e12e70138d81dd8c59fb6a2d6d16d9","number":15,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix docked tab bar pinning and catalog data regression introduced in PR #14","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"PR #14 failed to fix the docked tab bar and introduced a regression where catalog content stopped rendering. Root causes: (1) `ContentView`'s root `ZStack` never received full-screen bounds, so `CatalogView`'s `.safeAreaInset(edge: .bottom)` had no reliable anchor; (2) stacking multiple competing `.frame(maxHeight: .infinity)` on nested parent/child views caused `ScrollView`/`LazyVStack` content to collapse to zero height.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`ContentView.body`** — add `.frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)` to the root `ZStack`. This is the actual fix: full-screen bounds must be established at the true root for `safeAreaInset` to pin reliably.\n\n```swift\n// Before\nZStack { ... }\n.environmentObject(app)\n\n// After\nZStack { ... }\n.frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)\n.environmentObject(app)\n```\n\n- **`CatalogView.body`** — remove the two redundant frame modifiers added by PR #14 (`.frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity, alignment: .top)` on the inner `VStack` and `.frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)` on the outer `ZStack`). The single `.frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)` on the tab-content `Group` remains as the correct constraint level.\n\n- **`discoverContent` / `searchContent`** — remove the trailing `.frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity, alignment: .top)` from each `Group`. These competed with the parent `Group` frame, creating the ambiguous height that collapsed `ScrollView` content.\n\n> **Note:** CI cannot build SwiftUI (no Xcode/simulator; `swiftc -typecheck` fails on Linux with `error: no such module 'SwiftUI'`). Changes are validated against SwiftUI layout semantics — parent-driven sizing means one `maxHeight: .infinity` at the root propagates correctly; stacked `maxHeight: .infinity` on parent/child pairs causes the described collapse.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08T05:29:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-08T05:35:12Z","closed_at":"2026-08-08T